{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.DiagonalSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.DiagonalSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basis","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.eq_top_of_single_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.eq_top_of_single_mem","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/DiagonalSeparation.lean#L123-L133","doc":"**The matrix units generate everything.**  A subalgebra containing every `single i j 1` is all\nof `Matrix ι ι R`, since every matrix is the sum of its entries times the units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.single_self_mem_of_separating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.single_self_mem_of_separating","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/DiagonalSeparation.lean#L36-L121","doc":"**Separating diagonals generate the diagonal matrix units.**  If `A` contains\n`diagonal (d · v)` for every `v`, and the tuples `d i ·` separate the indices, then\n`single i i 1 ∈ A` for every `i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}